    "rawResponseText": "A **soft-brand hotel** is an independently designed and named hotel affiliated with a major hotel company.\n\nIt keeps its **unique identity, décor, and local character**, while gaining access to the parent company’s:\n\n- Reservation and distribution systems  \n- Loyalty program  \n- Marketing network  \n- Operational support and standards  \n\nFor example, an independent hotel might join **Curio Collection by Hilton** while retaining its original name and style. ([stories.hilton.com](https://stories.hilton.com/releases/hiltons-curio-and-tapestry-collections-celebrate-200th-hotel-milestones?utm_source=openai))\n\nCommon soft brands include:\n\n- **Marriott:** Autograph Collection, Tribute Portfolio, The Luxury Collection  \n- **Hilton:** Curio Collection, Tapestry Collection  \n- **Hyatt:** Unbound Collection  \n- **IHG:** Vignette Collection  \n- **Choice Hotels:** Ascend Hotel Collection  \n\nUnlike a traditional—or **hard-brand**—hotel, a soft-brand property doesn’t have to look and operate exactly like every other hotel in the chain.",
